  <div>
    <h3 class="inchy-feature-heading">PROTEIN. FIBER.<br>YOUR BODY’S OWN SIGNALS.</h3>
    <p class="inchy-era-line">Protein and certain dietary fibers can stimulate the body’s own release of GLP-1—a gut hormone involved in appetite regulation.</p>
    <p class="inchy-small">These are findings about particular nutrients and study preparations. They do not establish the GLP-1 response to a serving of INCHY.</p>
    <a class="inchy-text-link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=research#protein">PROTEIN &amp; FIBER EVIDENCE →</a>
  </div>
  <div class="inchy-research-preview__copy">
    <p class="inchy-kicker">A SEPARATE LABORATORY FINDING</p>
    <p>Peptides derived from sacha inchi meal inhibited DPP-IV in laboratory tests. DPP-IV is an enzyme that breaks down GLP-1.</p>
    <p class="inchy-small">Zhang et al. · 2023 · Laboratory study<br>This was not a human trial of finished {% render 'inchy-logo', inline: true %} and does not establish effects on appetite or GLP-1 in people taking INCHY.</p>
    <a class="inchy-text-link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}?view=research">EXPLORE THE EVIDENCE →</a>
